  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shaik Kalesha Vali vs The State Of Ap on 12 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4979 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 to A4 seek to quash the proceedings against them in C.C.No.251 of 2018 on the file of Additional Judicial First Class Magistrate, Addanki, which was taken cognizance for the offences under Sections 273 and 188 of IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 30.01.2018 at 17.45 hoursevening, when the complainant along with his staff rushed to the petitioner's/A1 Pan shop, found the banned tobacco products in his possession and on enquiry, he confessed that he purchased the same from A2 to A4 and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.17 of 2018 of Martur Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
